
Run from the project root:

    python test/run_host_tests.py
    python -m unittest discover -s test -p 'test_*calibration.py' -v

Requires g++ with C++17 on PATH. This runner compiles each actual sketch
separately against the hardware fakes in host/fakes, runs state-machine
assertions, and validates every emitted JSON line. Executables are placed
in the ignored .pio/host-tests directory. MW-1 is checked with the sketch's
current door-requirement setting, then with the opposite boolean initializer
in a generated sketch copy. The deployed firmware sources remain unchanged.

This is a host simulation, not a PlatformIO on-device test suite. It does
not open a serial port or upload firmware. Follow each sketch's hardware
bring-up checklist after building and uploading its own environment.

The Python tests cover press/release capture, chords and duplicate mappings,
extended GPIO assignments, concurrent source edit protection, fragmented
serial lines, raw event tracing and loss-of-heartbeat detection. They require
the same pyserial dependency as the operator scripts.
